## 🚀 Installation & Execution

### 1. Setup

```bash
# Clone and install
git clone https://github.com/Spidey44/MN-Coding-Exercise---Automate-demo.simplcommerce-with-Playwright.git
cd MN-Coding-Exercise---Automate-demo.simplcommerce-with-Playwright
npm install
npx playwright install chromium

### 2. Environment Configuration

BASE_URL=https://demo.simplcommerce.com
EMAIL_USER=your-email@example.com
PASS_USER=your-password

### 3. Test Suite Overview

The following tests are included as required by the assignment:

Cart Management
TC_CART_001: Adding a product to the cart.
TC_CART_002: Removing a product from the cart.
TC_CART_003: Updating product quantity (Data-Driven).

Checkout Flow
TC_CHECK_001: Proceeding to checkout with valid details.
TC_CHECK_010: Attempting checkout with missing/invalid details (no address / invalid payment).

### 4. Data-Driven Testing

Tests are scaled using data arrays to validate multiple products without code duplication:

const products = [
  { name: "iPhone 6s 16GB", url: "/iphone-6s-16gb", addClicks: 2 },
  { name: "Dell XPS 15 9550", url: "/dell-xps-15-9550", addClicks: 1 },
];

for (const item of products) {
  test(`Updating product quantity - ${item.name}`, async ({ page }) => {
    // Test logic here
  });
}


### 5. Run Tests

Run all the tests with: npx playwright test
Run all the test with UI: npx playwright test --headed
View HTML Execution Report: npx playwright show-report

### 6. CI/CD Pipeline

Tool: GitHub Actions (Ubuntu-latest).
Triggers: Automated on push and pull_request.
Security: Sensitive data handled via GitHub Secrets (BASE_URL, EMAIL_USER, PASS_USER).
Optimization: Focused on Chromium for fast feedback loops.
Artifacts: HTML reports stored for 30 days for debugging.
Workflow: .github/workflows/playwright.yml

